    {
      "id": "D893L4djrK39sztXetBHG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 213,
      "y": 166,
      "width": 590,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1251785909,
      "version": 320,
      "versionNonce": 1893789653,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786251901254,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. One of the 4 pillars of OOP.\n   Other three are:\n   --> Encapsulation\n   --> Polymorphism\n   --> Abstraction\n\n2. Inheritance means creating a new class from an existing\nclass,\n   where the new class inherits the properties and\nbehaviors\n   (data members and methods) of the existing class.\n\n3. Benefits:\n   --> Code reusability\n   --> Maintainability\n   --> Easy updation",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. One of the 4 pillars of OOP.\n   Other three are:\n   --> Encapsulation\n   --> Polymorphism\n   --> Abstraction\n\n2. Inheritance means creating a new class from an existing class,\n   where the new class inherits the properties and behaviors\n   (data members and methods) of the existing class.\n\n3. Benefits:\n   --> Code reusability\n   --> Maintainability\n   --> Easy updation",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "f6wVVzkYeo3rMxbZy-cK1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 359,
      "y": 631,
      "width": 220,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
