      "updated": 1786251914146,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Types of Inheritance\n====================\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Types of Inheritance\n====================\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aAI-e3FLLGm6-z2IAEfAQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 185,
      "y": 688,
      "width": 545,
      "height": 1875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 710511739,
      "version": 1727,
      "versionNonce": 405811867,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786253791830,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Types of Inheritance\n====================\n\nThere are 5 types of inheritance in OOPs:\n\n\n1. Single Inheritance\n\n   --> Supported by Java.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n2. Multilevel Inheritance\n\n   --> Supported by Java.\n\n\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n3. Multiple Inheritance\n\n   --> Not supported through classes in Java.\n   \n   --> Reason: Ambiguity problem.\n   \n   --> Suppose class A and class B both have a method\n       with the same name, and class C inherits from\nboth A and B.\n       \n                 \n                 \n                 \n                    \n       \n       If C calls that method, Java would not know\nwhether\n       to call A's method or B's method.\n       \n   --> This creates ambiguity, so Java does not\nsupport\n       multiple inheritance through classes.\n       \n   --> Java focuses on simplicity and avoids such\nambiguity.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n4. Hierarchial inheritance \n\n  --> supported by java\n\n  \n--> In this type, multiple child classes inherit from a\nsingle parent class. \n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n5. hybrib inheritance \n\n   --> not supported by java \n\n   --> to avoid diamond problem\n\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Types of Inheritance\n====================\n\nThere are 5 types of inheritance in OOPs:\n\n\n1. Single Inheritance\n\n   --> Supported by Java.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n2. Multilevel Inheritance\n\n   --> Supported by Java.\n\n\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n3. Multiple Inheritance\n\n   --> Not supported through classes in Java.\n   \n   --> Reason: Ambiguity problem.\n   \n   --> Suppose class A and class B both have a method\n       with the same name, and class C inherits from both A and B.\n       \n                 \n                 \n                 \n                    \n       \n       If C calls that method, Java would not know whether\n       to call A's method or B's method.\n       \n   --> This creates ambiguity, so Java does not support\n       multiple inheritance through classes.\n       \n   --> Java focuses on simplicity and avoids such ambiguity.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n4. Hierarchial inheritance \n\n  --> supported by java\n\n  \n--> In this type, multiple child classes inherit from a single parent class. \n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n5. hybrib inheritance \n\n   --> not supported by java \n\n   --> to avoid diamond problem\n\n\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
