    {
      "id": "45ftXtpeEL8Sg3q9rptPU",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 194,
      "y": 5887,
      "width": 544,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b01",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 185567870,
      "version": 852,
      "versionNonce": 424176418,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786296775826,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. super is a keyword which is used in child class to\nrefer to the members of parent class .\n\n2. Using super beomes compulsory in two programming\nsituations .\n\n--> For calling contructor of parent class from child\nclass .\n\n--> for resolving method overriding .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. super is a keyword which is used in child class to refer to the members of parent class .\n\n2. Using super beomes compulsory in two programming situations .\n\n--> For calling contructor of parent class from child class .\n\n--> for resolving method overriding .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uHMQU5XLCIORvLPbNXbga",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 194.8457107706073,
      "y": 6331.1501137083915,
      "width": 577,
      "height": 1000,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b04",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 856809726,
      "version": 446,
      "versionNonce": 1311431870,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1786298202527,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "# Rule of Constructor Calling in Inheritance\n=============================================\n\n1. When both parent and child classes have constructors,\n   and we create an object of the child class, both\n   constructors will execute.\n\n2. For one child class object, both parent and child\n   constructors execute.\n\n3. First, the parent class constructor executes and then\n   the child class constructor executes.\n\n4. Constructor calling happens from child to parent,\n   but constructor execution happens from parent to child.\n\nExample:\n---------\nChild object creation\n        ↓\nChild constructor\n        ↓\nParent constructor is called\n        ↓\nParent constructor executes\n        ↓\nChild constructor executes\n\nTherefore:\n\nCalling direction  → Child → Parent\nExecution order   → Parent → Child\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "# Rule of Constructor Calling in Inheritance\n=============================================\n\n1. When both parent and child classes have constructors,\n   and we create an object of the child class, both\n   constructors will execute.\n\n2. For one child class object, both parent and child\n   constructors execute.\n\n3. First, the parent class constructor executes and then\n   the child class constructor executes.\n\n4. Constructor calling happens from child to parent,\n   but constructor execution happens from parent to child.\n\nExample:\n---------\nChild object creation\n        ↓\nChild constructor\n        ↓\nParent constructor is called\n        ↓\nParent constructor executes\n        ↓\nChild constructor executes\n\nTherefore:\n\nCalling direction  → Child → Parent\nExecution order   → Parent → Child\n\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
